ILX:0794951 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lateral cutaneous nerve of the forearm" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The lateral cutaneous nerve of forearm (or lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve) is a sensory nerve representing the continuation of the musculocutaneous nerve beyond the lateral edge of the tendon of the biceps brachii muscle. The lateral antebrachial cutaneous nerve provides sensory innervation to the skin of the lateral forearm. It pierces the deep fascia of forearm to enter the subcutaneous compartment before splitting into a volar branch and a dorsal branch. It is derived from C5, C6 ventral rami." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0002386 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794951 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0794952 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Medial cutaneous nerve of the arm" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The medial cutaneous nerve of the arm (also known as the medial brachial cutaneous nerve and the lesser internal cutaneous nerve) is a sensory branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus derived from spinal nerves C8-T1. It provides sensory innervation to the lower portion of the medial arm. It descends accompanied by the basilic vein." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001814 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794952 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0003433 .

ILX:0794953 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "medial cutaneous nerve of the forearm" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The medial cutaneous nerve of the forearm (also known as the medial antebrachial cutaneous nerve) is a sensory branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus derived from the ventral rami of spinal nerves C8-T1. It provides sensory innervation to the skin of the medial forearm." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001814,
        UBERON:0003433 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794953 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0794967 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "posterior interosseous nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The continuation of the deep branch of the radial nerve after traversing the supinator muscle, supplying most extensor muscles of the forearm." ;
    ILX:0112785 ILX:0794977 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794967 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Posterior antebrachial interosseous nerve" .

ILX:0794979 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dorsal scapular nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The dorsal scapular nerve is a branch of the brachial plexus, usually derived from the ventral ramus of cervical nerve C5. It provides motor innervation to the rhomboid major muscle, rhomboid minor muscle, and sometimes the levator scapulae muscle." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001814 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794979 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0794996 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Ilioinguinal nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The ilioinguinal nerve is a branch of the first lumbar nerve (L1). The ilioinguinal nerve then perforates the transversus abdominis near the anterior part of the iliac crest, and communicates with the iliohypogastric nerve between the transversus and the internal oblique muscle." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0034987 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794996 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0794999 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Lateral cutaneous nerve of thigh" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The lateral cutaneous nerve of the thigh (also called the lateral femoral cutaneous nerve) is a cutaneous nerve of the thigh. It originates from the second and third lumbar nerves which are derived from the lumbar plexus. It passes under the inguinal ligament to reach the thigh. It supplies sensation to the skin on the lateral part of the thigh by an anterior branch and a posterior branch. It is derived from the ventral rami of L2 and L3." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0034987 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794999 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0795002 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "iliohypogastric nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The iliohypogastric nerve is a nerve that originates from the lumbar plexus that supplies sensation to skin over the lateral gluteal and hypogastric regions and motor to the internal oblique muscles and transverse abdominal muscles. It is derived from the ventral ramus of L1. It is a branch of the lumbar plexus that provides sensory innervation to the skin of the gluteal region and lower abdomen, as well as motor control to key muscles of the lower abdominal wall" ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0034987 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795002 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0795005 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Posterior cutaneous nerve of arm" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The posterior cutaneous nerve of arm (also known as posterior brachial cutaneous nerve) is a branch of the radial nerve that provides sensory innervation for much of the skin on the back of the arm. It is derived from the ventral rami of C5, C6, C7, and C8." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001492 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795005 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0003433 .

ILX:0795007 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "superior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The superior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm (or superior lateral brachial cutaneous nerve) is the continuation of the posterior branch of the axillary nerve, after it pierces the deep fascia. It is derived from the ventral rami of C5 and C6." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001493 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795007 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ILX:0797544 .

ILX:0795018 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "proper palmar digital branches of median nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Proper palmar digital nerves arise from the common digital branches of the median nerve and innervate the lateral 3 digits and the lateral side of the ring (4th) digit." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001148 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795018 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001027 .

ILX:0795021 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Inferior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The inferior lateral cutaneous nerve of arm is a nerve found in humans and other animals. It is also called the inferior lateral brachial cutaneous nerve. It is a branch of the radial nerve that provides sensory and vasomotor innervation to the lower, lateral aspect of the arm.  It is derived from the ventral rami of C5 and C6." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001492 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795021 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ILX:0797544 .

ILX:0795283 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "first intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The anatomical space between the first and second ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321185,
        ILX:0795283 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795284 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "infraclavicular fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A small triangular depression located inferior to the clavicle, bounded by the clavicle, deltoid, and pectoralis major muscles." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/infraclavicular-fossa-1536888660" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:61541,
        ILX:0795284 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795285 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anterior median line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A vertical line running along the midline of the anterior body surface, aligned with the sternum. On the anterior abdominal and chest walls, the anterior median line can be seen extending from the jugular notch, crossing over the sternum and linea alba in their midline, and reaching out to the midline pubic symphysis." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/anterior-median-line-1536887700" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20310,
        ILX:0795285 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795286 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "clavipectoral triangle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A triangular region bounded by the clavicle superiorly, the pectoralis major medially, and the deltoid laterally." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008785 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clavipectoral_triangle" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795286 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795287 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anterior axillary fold" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The anterior boundary of the axilla, formed by the lower border of the pectoralis major muscle." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/anterior-axillary-fold-1536887752" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:322184,
        ILX:0795287 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795288 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dorsal wrist" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The posterior aspect of the wrist, containing the extensor tendons and underlying carpal bones." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008785 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.uptodate.com/contents/anatomy-and-basic-biomechanics-of-the-wrist" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:24924,
        ILX:0795288 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795289 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "radial fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The radial fossa, also called the anatomical snuffbox, is a triangular depression on the lateral wrist. It is bordered by the tendons of the extensor pollicis longus, extensor pollicis brevis, and abductor pollicis longus, with the scaphoid and trapezium forming its floor. It houses the radial artery and is clinically relevant for assessing scaphoid fractures or arterial pulse." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001461 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/radial-fossa-1537018612" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:23452,
        ILX:0795289 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795290 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "nasolabial sulcus" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A shallow groove extending from the lateral aspect of the nostril to the corner of the mouth." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001456 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/nasolabial-sulcus-1536888784" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:75018,
        ILX:0795290 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000093 .

ILX:0795291 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mandibular notch" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The mandibular notch, also known as the sigmoid notch, is a groove in the ramus of the mandible. A curved depression between the coronoid and condylar processes of the mandible." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0003129 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mandibular_notch" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:59481,
        ILX:0795291 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795292 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "anterior hairline" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The demarcation at the anterior margin of the scalp where hair growth begins." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000033 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.semanticscholar.org/topic/Anterior-hairline/3368103" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:285414,
        ILX:0795292 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795293 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lesser supraclavicular fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A small depression located superior to the clavicle and medial to the clavicular head of the sternocleidomastoid muscle." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/lesser-supraclavicular-fossa-1536888804" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:84981,
        ILX:0795293 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795294 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "greater supraclavicular fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The greater supraclavicular fossa refers to the larger, lateral depression above the clavicle, located lateral to the sternocleidomastoid muscle." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/greater-supraclavicular-fossa-1536888404" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:84958,
        ILX:0795294 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795295 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "second intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The anatomical space between the second and third ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321188,
        ILX:0795295 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795296 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "sternal angle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The sternal angle (angle of Louis, Ludwig, or Ludovicus) is the inclined junction between the anterior surfaces of the manubrium and body of the sternum." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/skeletal-system/axial-skeleton/sternal-angle/18493" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:7547,
        ILX:0795296 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795297 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "third intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The space between the third and fourth ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321191,
        ILX:0795297 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795298 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fourth intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The space between the fourth and fifth ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321195,
        ILX:0795298 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795299 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fifth intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The space between the fifth and sixth ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321198,
        ILX:0795299 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795300 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "nipple line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The nipple line is an imaginary horizontal reference line running around the body at the level of the nipples." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/mammillary-line-1536888320" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20304,
        ILX:0795300 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795301 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "upper abdomen" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The superior portion of the abdomen, located above the umbilicus and below the ribcage." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.britannica.com/science/abdominal-cavity" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20364,
        ILX:0795301 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795302 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "infrasternal angle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The infrasternal angle (subcostal angle) is formed in front of thoracic cage by the cartilages of the tenth, ninth, eighth, and seventh ribs, which ascend on either side, where the apex of which the xiphoid process projects." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/infrasternal-angle-1537019816" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:7573,
        ILX:0795302 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795303 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lower abdomen" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The inferior portion of the abdomen, located below the umbilicus and above the pelvic region." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.britannica.com/science/abdominal-cavity" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20365,
        ILX:0795303 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795304 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "rectus femoris muscle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The rectus femoris is a muscle in the anterior compartment of the thigh. It forms part of the quadriceps femoris muscle complex, and is the only muscle in this group to cross both the hip joint and the knee joints." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008784 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rectus_femoris_muscle" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795304 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001630 .

ILX:0795305 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "medial malleolus" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A prominent bony projection on the medial aspect of the distal tibia, forming part of the ankle joint." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008784 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/medial-malleolus-1537020872" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:35451,
        ILX:0795305 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795306 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lateral thoracic region" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The area of the thorax on the lateral body wall, containing portions of the serratus anterior and intercostal muscles." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/lateral-region-of-thorax-1536888820" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:61533,
        ILX:0795306 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795307 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "sixth intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The space between the sixth and seventh ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321201,
        ILX:0795307 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795308 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "midaxillary line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A vertical line running down the lateral thorax from the apex of the axilla to the hip." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/midaxillary-line-1536888352" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:14368,
        ILX:0795308 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795309 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "axillary fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A pyramidal depression located at the junction of the upper limb and thorax, commonly referred to as the armpit." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008785 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/axillary-fossa-1536889648" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:61464,
        ILX:0795309 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795310 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cubital fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A triangular depression on the anterior aspect of the elbow, containing important neurovascular structures." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001460 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cubital_fossa" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:39848,
        ILX:0795310 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795311 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "posterior axillary fold" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The posterior axillary fold, also known as the posterior armpit fold, refers to the inferior border of the posterior wall of axilla." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008785 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/posterior-axillary-fold-1536887776" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:322185,
        ILX:0795311 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795312 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "posterior median line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A vertical line running along the posterior midline of the back, aligned with the spinous processes of the vertebrae." ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/posterior-median-line-1536888480" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20311,
        ILX:0795312 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795313 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "first posterior sacral foramen" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The first opening in the posterior sacrum, allowing passage of sacral nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0005473 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/nervous-system/peripheral-nervous-system/posterior-root-of-first-sacral-nerve/17108" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:31769,
        ILX:0795313 ;
