    IAO:0000115 "The second opening in the posterior sacrum for sacral nerve passage." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0005473 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/nervous-system/peripheral-nervous-system/posterior-root-of-first-sacral-nerve/17108" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:31770,
        ILX:0795314 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795315 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "third posterior sacral foramen" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The third opening in the posterior sacrum for sacral nerve passage." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0005473 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/nervous-system/peripheral-nervous-system/posterior-root-of-first-sacral-nerve/17108" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:31771,
        ILX:0795315 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795316 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fourth posterior sacral foramen" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The fourth opening in the posterior sacrum for sacral nerve passage." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0005473 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/nervous-system/peripheral-nervous-system/posterior-root-of-first-sacral-nerve/17108" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:31772,
        ILX:0795316 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795317 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "biceps femoris tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The biceps femoris tendon is the rounded tendon that attaches the muscle bellies of the long and short heads of the biceps femoris muscle to the head of the fibula." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008784 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/muscular-system/muscles-of-lower-limb/biceps-femoris-tendon/22415" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:45930,
        ILX:0795317 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795318 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "fourth metacarpal bone" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The long bone in the hand that connects the fourth finger to the carpal bones of the wrist. The fourth metacarpal bone is shorter and smaller than the third. The base is small and quadrilateral." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001442 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/metacarpal-iv-121123560" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795318 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001474 .

ILX:0795321 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "seventh intercostal space" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The anatomical space between the seventh and eighth ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intercostal_space" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:321204,
        ILX:0795321 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0012198 .

ILX:0795322 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "midclavicular line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Midclavicular line is an important vertical reference line on the anterior chest wall. It connects the midclavicular point (superiorly) with the middle of the inguinal ligament (inferiorly)." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/midclavicular-line-15368877400" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20251,
        ILX:0795322 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795323 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "posterior axillary line" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Posterior axillary line is an imaginary reference line which can be drawn on the posterior torso. It extends vertically downwards from the posterior axillary fold. The posterior axillary line runs in parallel to the midaxillary and anterior axillary lines." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001443 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/posterior-axillary-line-1536888360" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:20260,
        ILX:0795323 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795324 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "iliotibial band" ;
    IAO:0000115 "Your iliotibial band is a strong, thick band of tissue that runs down the outside of your thigh. It extends all the way from the hip bone to the top of the shinbone." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0008784 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iliotibial_tract" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:51048,
        ILX:0795324 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795325 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "tibialis anterior tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tibialis anterior tendon is the tendon of the tibialis anterior muscle, located on the front of the lower leg. It passes along the ankle and inserts on the medial cuneiform and the first metatarsal. This tendon enables dorsiflexion and inversion of the foot. The tibialis anterior tendon (TAT) begins at the distal one-third of the tibia. It is the most medial tendon of the ankle and foot." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000978 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tibialis_anterior_muscle" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:47050,
        ILX:0795325 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795326 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "posterior hairline" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The demarcation at the posterior margin of the scalp where hair growth begins, near the nape of the neck." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000033 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/medgen/868215" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:285422,
        ILX:0795326 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0006800 .

ILX:0795327 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "mentolabial sulcus" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The mentolabial sulcus is the vertical groove or fold that forms between the lower lip and the chin, marking the transition between the lower lip and the mental region of the face." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001456 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.imaios.com/en/e-anatomy/anatomical-structure/mentolabial-sulcus-1536888420" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:75019,
        ILX:0795327 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000093 .

ILX:0795328 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "hyoid tubercle" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A small prominence on the posterior end of the greater horn of hyoid bone, serving as an attachment point for muscles and ligaments. Each tubercle of hyoid bone provides an attachment site for a lateral thyrohyoid ligament." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hyoid_bone" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795328 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795329 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "inguinal crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The inguinal crease refers to the skin fold or line that forms where the lower abdomen meets the thigh, often most noticeable when the hip is flexed. It marks the boundary between the abdominal and thigh regions." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000916 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/medicine-and-dentistry/inguinal-region" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795329 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795330 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "popliteal crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "This is the visible skin fold or line at the back of the knee, formed when the knee is flexed. It is a superficial feature and serves as a landmark for the location of the popliteal fossa beneath." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000978 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popliteal_fossa" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795330 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

ILX:0795331 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "suprasternal fossa" ;
    IAO:0000115 "This is the depression on the skin surface of the neck between the sternal heads of the sternocleidomastoid muscles. This area is situated just above the manubrium of the sternum and is a visible landmark in the neck." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0000974 ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suprasternal_notch" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795331 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004704 .

ILX:0795332 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "cubital crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The anterior skin fold of the elbow, marking the transition between the upper arm and forearm, overlying the cubital fossa." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795332 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0019243 .

ILX:0795333 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "dorsal wrist crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The dorsal wrist crease is the skin fold that forms on the back (dorsal) side of the wrist, often visible when the hand is extended. It marks the junction between the forearm and the hand and is located near the proximal ends of the metacarpal bones." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795333 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0019243 .

ILX:0795334 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "palmar wrist crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The palmar wrist crease is the transverse skin fold that appears on the palm side of the wrist when the hand is flexed. It marks the boundary between the forearm and the palm and is located approximately at the level of the distal radius and ulna." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795334 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0019243 .

ILX:0795335 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "abductor pollicis longus tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle that abducts and extends the thumb, located in the posterior compartment of the forearm." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795335 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795336 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "extensor pollicis brevis tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle extending the proximal phalanx of the thumb, positioned laterally in the forearm." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795336 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795337 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "extensor pollicis longus tendon" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The tendon of the muscle responsible for extending the thumb at the interphalangeal joint." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0795337 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0000043 .

ILX:0795338 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "lateral supraepicondylar ridge" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The lateral supracondylar ridge (lateral supraepicondylar ridge or lateral supracondylar crest) is the sharp, prominent margin located along the lateral aspect of the distal end of the body of the humerus. It is the less curved of the two supracondylar ridges of the humerus, the other being the medial supracondylar ridge." ;
    ILX:0777130 "https://www.elsevier.com/resources/anatomy/skeletal-system/appendicular-skeleton/lateral-supracondylar-ridge/18104" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId FMA:75078,
        ILX:0795338 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001062 .

