UBERON:0019243 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "skin crease" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A skin crease (anatomically known as a flexure line or skin furrow) is a permanent, fixed linear depression on the surface of the skin that is directly attached to the underlying deep tissues, fascia, or joints. Source: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27081433/" ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId UBERON:0019243,
        ILX:0736980 ;
    oboInOwl:hasDbXref "http://www.snomedbrowser.com/Codes/Details/280385004" ;
    oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym "skin groove" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:3000961 .

ILX:0794966 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "suprascapular nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "A branch of the upper trunk of the brachial plexus (C5-C6) supplying the supraspinatus and infraspinatus muscles and contributing articular branches to the shoulder." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001814,
        ILX:0794966 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794966 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 ;
    oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym "Nervus suprascapularis" .

ILX:0794975 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "medial pectoral nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The medial pectoral nerve (also known as the medial anterior thoracic nerve) is (typically) a branch of the medial cord of the brachial plexus and is derived from ventral rami  C8-T1. It provides motor innervation to the pectoralis minor muscle, and part of the pectoralis major muscle." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001814,
        ILX:0794975 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794975 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0794977 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "deep branch of radial nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The radial nerve divides into a superficial (sensory) and deep (motor) branch at the cubital fossa. The deep branch of the radial nerve winds to the back of the forearm around the lateral side of the radius between the two planes of fibers of the supinator, and is prolonged downward between the superficial and deep layers of muscles, to the middle of the forearm. The deep branch and its continuation, called the posterior interosseous nerve, provides motor function to the muscles in the posterior compartment of the forearm, which are mostly the extensor muscles of the wrist and hand." ;
    ILX:0112785 UBERON:0001492,
        ILX:0794977 ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0794977 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0001021 .

ILX:0797544 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Lateral brachial cutaneous nerve" ;
    IAO:0000115 "The lateral brachial cutaneous nerve is a collective anatomical term for two distinct sensory nerves—the superior and inferior lateral brachial cutaneous nerves—that provide somatic sensation to the skin on the lateral (outer) aspect of the upper arm." ;
    ilxtr:hasExistingId ILX:0797544 ;
    rdfs:subClassOf UBERON:0004217 .

